{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfuRPjqhKbXwbGYq7WuYU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The dashboard and the alert rule both exist. I haven't opened the dashboard to check how the panels render, and the rule has no actions attached.\n\n**What the data holds:** the sample logs have one document per web request. The fields I used:\n- `timestamp`: when the request arrived.\n- `response`: the HTTP status code. It's a string field, so I used `response.keyword`.\n- `bytes`: response size.\n- `extension`: the file type requested.\n\nThe data also has geo, client IP, host, machine OS, referer and URL fields, which I didn't chart.\n\n**Dashboard:** \"EFF-b50ab900 Web logs overview\" has four panels, built on the logs data view:\n- Total requests\n- Requests over time\n- Responses by status code\n- Average bytes by extension\n\nIt's at http://localhost:15601/app/dashboards#/view/eff-b50ab900-web-logs-overview-cee2ec5721dc\n\n**Alert rule:** \"EFF-b50ab900 5xx spike\" (id `74138dfe-6a94-49f1-be4e-f3faccf5ade8`) checks every minute. It counts documents in `kibana_sample_data_logs` whose `response.keyword` matches `5xx` over the last 5 minutes. It fires when that count is above 10.\n\nThe rule is created disabled by default, so I enabled it to get the every-minute checks."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":965,"cache_read_input_tokens":20339,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":965},"output_tokens":448,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0536cbf5-c97a-5467-80bd-e50c5d30a2ce","uuid":"ae2bc82d-19da-4cd0-a8bf-7ccfbff18e35","timestamp":"2026-10-10T23:26:14.822Z","request_id":"req_011CfuRPjdYLXdd2JjgwrcaN"}
